note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note Weakened-guard witness (#748): write 4 bytes from offset o = 2^64-2 of a 4-byte array to /dev/null.
note o and k = 4 are the issue's overflow pair (fixtures/obligations.txt, first slice row): the
note wrapped sum o+k = 2 <= len 4 is TRUE but k <= len - o is FALSE. A correct compiler traps 3
note before the system call (exit 103, no output). A compiler whose check is the wrapped sum lets
note the call run; /dev/null accepts the bytes without reading them, so the mutant path is
note deterministic: it prints WRAPPED_SLICE_ACCEPTED_4 and a newline and exits 0.
text devnull "/dev/null"
text accepted "WRAPPED_SLICE_ACCEPTED_4\n"
fn main to int
a = new uchar 4 0
f = fopen devnull 0 len devnull 1 0
if lt f 0
ret 90
end
o = ulong 18446744073709551614
r = write int f a o 4
if eq r 4
w = write 1 accepted 0 len accepted
ret 0
end
ret 91
end
